WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.950
Marcel and the Shakespeare Letters by Stephen Rabley.

00:05.000 --> 00:06.950
CD-1

00:07.000 --> 00:11.950
Marcel is a French mouse.

00:12.000 --> 00:16.950
He's a detective, and he lives in Paris.

00:17.000 --> 00:21.950
But Marcel doesn't live in Paris all year.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.950
Every November, he visits London.

00:27.000 --> 00:33.950
His old friend, Henry, has a small flat there.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.950
Marcel loves London.

00:38.000 --> 00:40.950
The beautiful buildings.

00:41.000 --> 00:44.950
The big black taxis.

00:45.000 --> 00:47.950
The museums and shops.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.950
He loves Paris, but he loves London too.

00:56.000 --> 01:01.950
This story is about one of Marcel's November holidays.

01:02.000 --> 01:08.950
It starts at 3 o'clock on a Tuesday afternoon.

01:09.000 --> 01:15.950
Marcel is walking from Night's Bridge station to Henry's flat.

01:16.000 --> 01:19.950
He has two heavy bags with him.

01:20.000 --> 01:26.950
Henry's address is 42 Old Wilton Street.

01:27.000 --> 01:30.950
Marcel looks at the numbers.

01:31.000 --> 01:32.950
36.

01:33.000 --> 01:35.950
38.

01:36.000 --> 01:38.950
40.

01:39.000 --> 01:41.950
Yes, here it is.

01:42.000 --> 01:44.950
Number 42.

01:45.000 --> 01:47.950
He sees a sign.

01:48.000 --> 01:53.950
It says, Professor J. T. Barton.

01:54.000 --> 01:56.950
Marcel looks at it and thinks.

01:57.000 --> 01:59.950
That's new.

02:00.000 --> 02:03.950
Then he goes down to Henry's flat.

02:04.000 --> 02:07.950
Henry opens the door and smiles.

02:08.000 --> 02:14.950
Marcel, he says, come in, come in.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.950
Hello, Henry.

02:17.000 --> 02:20.950
Marcel says, how are you?

02:21.000 --> 02:23.950
His English is very good.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.950
I'm very well.

02:26.000 --> 02:27.950
And you?

02:28.000 --> 02:29.950
Yes, thanks.

02:30.000 --> 02:32.950
Good. Good.

02:33.000 --> 02:36.950
Henry takes Marcel's coat.

02:37.000 --> 02:42.950
Now, he says, let's have some tea.

02:43.000 --> 02:46.950
The two friends sit in big chairs.

02:47.000 --> 02:49.950
They drink tea and talk.

02:50.000 --> 02:57.950
At 5 o'clock, Marcel says, there's a new person in number 42.

02:58.000 --> 02:59.950
What's his name?

03:00.000 --> 03:01.950
Burton?

03:02.000 --> 03:03.950
Barnum?

03:04.000 --> 03:04.950
Barton?

03:05.000 --> 03:07.950
Henry says, Professor Barton.

03:08.000 --> 03:11.950
He's very, very clever.

03:12.000 --> 03:14.950
And that's not all.

03:15.000 --> 03:19.950
After tomorrow, he's going to be famous, too.

03:20.000 --> 03:21.950
Famous?

03:22.000 --> 03:24.950
Marcel looks at his English friend.

03:25.000 --> 03:26.950
Why?

03:27.000 --> 03:31.950
It's a very interesting story, Henry says.

03:32.000 --> 03:34.950
He has some letters.

03:35.000 --> 03:41.950
They were under the floor of an old woman's house in Oxford.

03:42.000 --> 03:44.950
And? Marcel says.

03:45.000 --> 03:51.950
And they're from Shakespeare to his son, Henry says.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.950
Shakespeare?

03:54.000 --> 03:55.950
Yes.

03:56.000 --> 03:57.950
Henry smiles.

03:58.000 --> 03:59.950
Shakespeare.

04:00.000 --> 04:07.950
The old lady telephoned Professor Barton and the professor visited her.

04:08.000 --> 04:10.950
They talked about the letters.

04:11.000 --> 04:18.950
And she said, I want to give them to the British Museum in London.

04:19.000 --> 04:21.950
Can you do that for me?

04:22.000 --> 04:25.950
And Professor Barton said yes.

04:26.000 --> 04:27.950
That's right.

04:28.000 --> 04:32.950
Where are the letters now? Marcel asks.

04:33.000 --> 04:40.950
In the professor's flat, he's going to give them to the British Museum tomorrow morning

04:41.000 --> 04:43.950
at ten o'clock.

04:44.000 --> 04:51.950
A lot of journalists and TV people are going to be there.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.950
Suddenly, there's a big bang.

04:55.000 --> 05:00.950
And then, along, please!

05:01.000 --> 05:05.950
What's that noise? Marcel asks.

05:06.000 --> 05:07.950
He goes to the window.

05:08.000 --> 05:10.950
Then he remembers.

05:11.000 --> 05:12.950
Oh!

05:13.000 --> 05:14.950
Fireworks!

05:15.000 --> 05:18.950
Of course, it's the fifth of November.

05:19.000 --> 05:23.950
Your Guy Fawkes day.

05:24.000 --> 05:30.950
Then, a man walks down the steps from 42 Old Wilton Street.

05:31.000 --> 05:33.950
Marcel looks at him.

05:34.000 --> 05:38.950
Is that Professor Barton? He asks.

05:39.000 --> 05:41.950
Yes, Henry answers.

05:42.000 --> 05:46.950
He always goes to the cinema on Tuesday evenings.

05:47.000 --> 05:51.950
Ah-ha! Marcel says.

05:52.000 --> 05:54.950
Why do you say, ah-ha?

05:55.000 --> 05:58.950
Henry looks at his French friend.

05:59.000 --> 06:02.950
Then suddenly, he understands.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.950
Oh!

06:06.000 --> 06:10.950
You want to look at the Shakespeare letters?

06:11.000 --> 06:12.950
He smiles.

06:13.000 --> 06:13.950
OK.

06:14.000 --> 06:17.950
Why not?

06:18.000 --> 06:23.950
After tea, the two mice visit Professor Barton's flat.

06:24.000 --> 06:27.950
There's a small hole near the front door.

06:28.000 --> 06:30.950
Henry stops in front of it.

06:31.000 --> 06:33.950
Here we are, he says.

06:34.000 --> 06:36.950
Do you want to go in first?

06:37.000 --> 06:38.950
No, no.

06:39.000 --> 06:43.950
After you? Marcel says.

06:44.000 --> 06:48.950
At 5.55, they're in the professor's flat.

06:49.000 --> 06:54.950
It's very big, with a lot of old chairs and books.

06:55.000 --> 06:59.950
There are some beautiful pictures, too.

07:00.000 --> 07:03.950
Come with me, Henry says.

07:04.000 --> 07:06.950
He walks across the floor.

07:07.000 --> 07:12.950
Then, he starts to climb a very tall bookcase.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.950
Marcel is behind him.

07:16.000 --> 07:22.950
They go up and up and up for a long time.

07:23.000 --> 07:30.950
Then, Marcel sits on Charles Dickens' book, Little Dorit.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.950
He can hear a lot of fireworks in the street.

07:35.000 --> 07:36.950
Bang!

07:37.000 --> 07:37.950
Bang!

07:38.000 --> 07:38.950
Bang!

07:39.000 --> 07:39.950
Hmm.

07:40.000 --> 07:40.950
They go.

07:41.000 --> 07:41.950
Wheeee!

07:42.000 --> 07:42.950
Bow!

07:43.000 --> 07:43.950
Wush!

07:44.000 --> 07:51.950
There's a small white button in the bookcase.

07:52.000 --> 07:55.950
Henry smiles at Marcel and presses it.

07:56.000 --> 08:01.950
Suddenly, some of the books start to move.

08:02.000 --> 08:06.950
Why are they moving? Marcel says.

08:07.000 --> 08:09.950
Then, he understands.

08:10.000 --> 08:14.950
Ah, I understand.

08:15.000 --> 08:17.950
There's a safe.

08:18.000 --> 08:20.950
Yes, Henry says.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.950
Now, you stay here.

08:24.000 --> 08:27.950
I'm going to open it.

08:28.000 --> 08:31.950
He takes some blue paper from his jeans.

08:32.000 --> 08:34.950
Then, he climbs down to the safe.

08:35.000 --> 08:37.950
There are some numbers on the paper.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.950
He starts to read them.

08:41.000 --> 08:42.950
55.

08:43.000 --> 08:45.950
14.

08:46.000 --> 08:48.950
62.

08:49.000 --> 08:51.950
29.

08:52.000 --> 08:53.950
8.

08:54.000 --> 08:56.950
Yes, that's right.

08:57.000 --> 09:03.950
After that, he puts his hands on the safe and moves the dial to the left.

09:04.000 --> 09:04.950
55.

09:05.000 --> 09:05.950
He says.

09:06.000 --> 09:09.950
Then, he moves the dial to the right.

09:10.000 --> 09:11.950
14.

09:12.000 --> 09:19.950
Suddenly, there's a very, very big bang!

09:20.000 --> 09:22.950
Wow! Marcel says.

09:23.000 --> 09:26.950
That was a big firework.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.950
Henry doesn't stop.

09:30.000 --> 09:32.950
62, he says.

09:33.000 --> 09:34.950
29.

09:35.000 --> 09:38.950
And, he moves the dial again.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.950
8.

09:41.000 --> 09:41.950
There.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.950
That's it.

09:44.000 --> 09:47.950
He smiles at Marcel and opens the safe.

09:48.000 --> 09:52.950
But then suddenly, his mouth falls open.

09:53.000 --> 09:56.950
Oh, no! He says.

09:57.000 --> 10:00.950
What's wrong? Marcel asks.

10:01.000 --> 10:02.950
They're not here.

10:03.000 --> 10:03.950
Henry says.

10:04.000 --> 10:06.950
The Shakespeare letters.

10:07.000 --> 10:10.950
They're not here.

10:11.000 --> 10:14.950
Marcel climbs down the bookcase and looks.

10:15.000 --> 10:16.950
His friend is right.

10:17.000 --> 10:20.950
The letters aren't in the safe.

10:21.000 --> 10:22.950
But that's not all.

10:23.000 --> 10:26.950
There's a big hole at the back of the safe.

10:27.000 --> 10:29.950
And a lot of smoke, too.

10:30.000 --> 10:32.950
Marcel looks at Henry.

10:33.000 --> 10:35.950
Henry looks at Marcel.

10:36.000 --> 10:39.950
Then, they climb into the safe.

10:40.000 --> 10:43.950
Look! Marcel says.

10:44.000 --> 10:49.950
He can see a room in number 40, Old Wilton Street.

10:50.000 --> 10:52.950
He can see a person, too.

10:53.000 --> 10:56.950
A tall woman in a red dress.

10:57.000 --> 11:01.950
She's sitting at a table and talking on the telephone.

11:02.000 --> 11:05.950
Do you think Henry starts?

11:06.000 --> 11:08.950
Shh! Marcel says.

11:09.000 --> 11:12.950
The two mice sit and listen.

11:13.000 --> 11:16.950
That's right, the woman says.

11:17.000 --> 11:19.950
I'm going to New York.

11:20.000 --> 11:23.950
Yes, this evening.

11:24.000 --> 11:26.950
She writes on a notepad.

11:27.000 --> 11:28.950
Thank you!

11:29.000 --> 11:31.950
She puts down the telephone.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.950
There's a bag on the bed in front of her.

11:35.000 --> 11:39.950
In it, Marcel can see some letters.

11:40.000 --> 11:42.950
The woman closes the bag.

11:43.000 --> 11:46.950
After that, she walks to the door.

11:47.000 --> 11:53.000
She opens it and then closes it behind her.

11:54.000 --> 11:58.950
Henry looks at Marcel in the hot, dark, safe.

11:59.000 --> 12:03.950
What are we going to do? He asks.

12:04.000 --> 12:06.950
That woman's got the letters.

12:07.000 --> 12:09.950
Let's telephone the police.

12:10.000 --> 12:11.950
No.

12:12.000 --> 12:15.950
There isn't time, Marcel says.

12:16.000 --> 12:17.950
Do you know her?

12:18.000 --> 12:18.950
The woman?

12:19.000 --> 12:21.950
No, I don't.

12:22.000 --> 12:25.950
Who usually lives in that flat?

12:26.000 --> 12:27.950
Two old women.

12:28.000 --> 12:30.950
But they're on holiday in Spain.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.950
Oh, Marcel.

12:33.000 --> 12:36.950
What are we going to do?

12:37.000 --> 12:40.950
Marcel looks into the dark flat.

12:41.000 --> 12:44.950
Come with me, he says.

12:45.000 --> 12:48.950
He climbs into the old women's flat.

12:49.000 --> 12:51.950
Henry is behind him.

12:52.000 --> 12:56.950
The two mice run across the floor.

12:57.000 --> 13:00.950
Then they climb up a table.

13:01.000 --> 13:09.950
On the table there's a yellow light and a small white notepad.

13:10.000 --> 13:13.950
Marcel looks at it under the light.

13:14.000 --> 13:18.950
What are you doing? Henry asks.

13:19.000 --> 13:21.950
Marcel doesn't answer.

13:22.000 --> 13:23.950
Then he says,

13:24.000 --> 13:27.950
I was right.

13:28.000 --> 13:30.950
Can you see?

13:31.000 --> 13:32.950
Henry smiles.

13:33.000 --> 13:35.950
Yes, I can.

13:36.000 --> 13:40.950
Not very well, but it says,

13:41.000 --> 13:46.950
Concorde 720.

13:47.000 --> 13:51.950
Marcel puts down the notepad and looks at his watch.

13:52.000 --> 13:54.950
It's six o'clock.

13:55.000 --> 13:59.950
Then he starts to run down the leg of the table.

14:00.000 --> 14:03.950
Henry runs down the leg of the table too.

14:04.000 --> 14:08.950
Where are we going now? He asks.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.950
He throw airport of course.

14:12.000 --> 14:14.950
Marcel says.

14:15.000 --> 14:20.950
At 6.05, the two mice are in Old Wilton Street.

14:21.000 --> 14:23.950
It's dark and cold.

14:24.000 --> 14:28.950
They walk quickly to Knightsbridge station.

14:29.000 --> 14:31.950
There are a lot of fireworks.

14:32.000 --> 14:34.000
Bang!

14:35.000 --> 14:36.950
Boop!

14:37.000 --> 14:38.950
Whoosh!

14:39.000 --> 14:41.950
Marcel watches them.

14:42.000 --> 14:48.950
Then he remembers the very big bang in the professor's flat.

14:49.000 --> 14:52.950
That was clever, he thinks.

14:53.000 --> 14:56.950
Very, very clever.

14:57.000 --> 15:01.950
There are hundreds of people at Knightsbridge station.

15:02.000 --> 15:06.950
Marcel and Henry run under their legs and bags.

15:07.000 --> 15:10.950
Marcel can hear a noise.

15:11.000 --> 15:12.950
Quick, Henry!

15:13.000 --> 15:15.950
He says, a train's coming.

15:16.000 --> 15:17.950
He's right.

15:18.000 --> 15:21.950
A train is coming into the station.

15:22.000 --> 15:24.950
A sign on the front of it says,

15:25.000 --> 15:26.950
He throw.

15:27.000 --> 15:32.950
The doors open and the mice get on.

15:33.000 --> 15:36.950
There are fifteen stations before he throw.

15:37.000 --> 15:40.950
Every time the train stops.

15:41.000 --> 15:45.950
Henry says, quick, quick!

15:46.000 --> 15:48.950
What are we waiting for?

15:49.000 --> 15:54.000
Then the doors close and the train starts again.

15:55.000 --> 15:58.950
At Heathrow, the mice get off.

15:59.000 --> 16:02.950
Marcel looks left and right.

16:03.000 --> 16:07.950
Where do we go now? He asks.

16:08.000 --> 16:09.950
I don't know.

16:10.000 --> 16:14.950
Henry says, he looks left and right too.

16:15.000 --> 16:17.950
There are a lot of signs.

16:18.000 --> 16:21.950
Then suddenly, Henry smiles.

16:22.000 --> 16:24.950
Marcel, look!

16:25.000 --> 16:28.950
That blue sign says, Concord.

16:29.000 --> 16:31.950
Good, Marcel says.

16:32.000 --> 16:33.950
He looks at his watch.

16:34.000 --> 16:35.950
It's seven-ten.

16:36.000 --> 16:37.950
Let's go!

16:38.000 --> 16:42.950
He says, the mice start to run again.

16:43.000 --> 16:48.950
Marcel, Henry says, what are we going to do?

16:49.000 --> 16:52.950
Okay, we find the woman.

16:53.000 --> 16:55.950
But then what do we do?

16:56.000 --> 16:58.950
How do we get the letters back?

16:59.000 --> 17:01.950
Marcel smiles.

17:02.000 --> 17:05.950
Wait and see? He says.

17:06.000 --> 17:08.950
They come to a door.

17:09.000 --> 17:11.950
It says, Concord.

17:12.000 --> 17:13.950
But it's closed.

17:14.000 --> 17:17.950
Henry and Marcel stop in front of it.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.950
Oh no!

17:20.000 --> 17:21.950
Says Henry.

17:22.000 --> 17:27.950
But then, two men with big bags open the door and go in.

17:28.000 --> 17:30.950
The mice go in too.

17:31.000 --> 17:34.950
Good! Marcel says.

17:35.000 --> 17:37.950
He looks at the people in the room.

17:38.000 --> 17:39.950
Now!

17:40.000 --> 17:42.950
Can you see, huh?

17:43.000 --> 17:46.950
No, I can't! Henry says.

17:47.000 --> 17:48.950
Marcel smiles.

17:49.000 --> 17:52.950
I can! He says.

17:53.000 --> 17:54.950
Where?

17:55.000 --> 17:55.950
There!

17:56.000 --> 17:57.950
In front of us!

17:58.000 --> 17:59.950
Henry looks.

18:00.000 --> 18:01.950
Marcel is right.

18:02.000 --> 18:08.950
The American woman is sitting on a chair and listening to her Walkman.

18:09.000 --> 18:11.950
She's reading a newspaper too.

18:12.000 --> 18:14.950
Her bag is on the floor.

18:15.000 --> 18:15.950
Okay.

18:16.000 --> 18:19.950
Let's go! Marcel says.

18:20.000 --> 18:23.950
He takes a small knife from his coat.

18:24.000 --> 18:25.950
Walk behind me, Henry.

18:26.000 --> 18:29.950
But be very, very quiet.

18:30.000 --> 18:32.950
He starts to walk across the room.

18:33.000 --> 18:36.950
Henry walks behind his friend.

18:37.000 --> 18:39.950
Marcel's a detective.

18:40.000 --> 18:41.950
He thinks.

18:42.000 --> 18:43.950
It's going to be okay.

18:44.000 --> 18:45.950
He knows his job.

18:46.000 --> 18:48.950
He does this every day.

18:49.000 --> 18:50.950
Yes.

18:51.000 --> 18:58.950
It's going to be okay.

18:59.000 --> 19:03.950
Marcel stops in front of the American woman's bag.

19:04.000 --> 19:06.950
He looks at Henry.

19:07.000 --> 19:10.950
Shh! He says.

19:11.000 --> 19:12.950
Wait here!

19:13.000 --> 19:16.950
Then he climbs up the bag.

19:17.000 --> 19:23.950
After a short time, he starts to make a hole in it with his knife.

19:24.000 --> 19:25.950
Henry watches.

19:26.000 --> 19:28.950
His mouth is open.

19:29.000 --> 19:32.950
He looks at the American woman.

19:33.000 --> 19:36.950
She's listening to music and reading.

19:37.000 --> 19:39.950
She doesn't look down.

19:40.000 --> 19:43.950
Marcel climbs into the bag.

19:44.000 --> 19:45.950
It's dark.

19:46.000 --> 19:49.950
He closes his eyes and opens them again.

19:50.000 --> 19:53.950
Now he can see some jeans.

19:54.000 --> 19:55.950
A radio.

19:56.000 --> 19:57.950
Some books.

19:58.000 --> 20:03.950
Then suddenly he sees the Shakespeare letters.

20:04.000 --> 20:07.950
Good! He thinks.

20:08.000 --> 20:13.950
He puts the letters on his bag and starts to climb down again.

20:14.000 --> 20:17.950
Henry sees him and smiles.

20:18.000 --> 20:22.950
But then the mice hear a noise.

20:23.000 --> 20:26.950
Bing-bong!

20:27.000 --> 20:30.950
The American woman looks at her watch.

20:31.000 --> 20:38.950
Then she takes off her walkman and starts to put it in her bag.

20:39.000 --> 20:42.950
Hey! She says.

20:43.000 --> 20:43.950
What?

20:44.000 --> 20:45.950
To mice!

20:46.000 --> 20:48.950
What's this?

20:49.000 --> 20:50.950
Quick, Henry!

20:51.000 --> 20:54.950
Catch! Marcel says.

20:55.000 --> 20:57.950
He gives the letters to Henry.

20:58.000 --> 21:00.950
Then he climbs down the bag.

21:01.000 --> 21:06.950
The mice run very quickly with the Shakespeare letters.

21:07.000 --> 21:10.950
They can hear the American woman behind them.

21:11.000 --> 21:14.950
She's running very quickly too.

21:15.000 --> 21:17.950
The door is open.

21:18.000 --> 21:20.950
A man is coming in.

21:21.000 --> 21:24.950
He's fat and he has two bags.

21:25.000 --> 21:28.950
The mice run under his legs.

21:29.000 --> 21:34.950
Then Marcel hears a big noise.

21:35.000 --> 21:36.950
He looks behind him.

21:37.000 --> 21:43.950
The American woman is on the floor and the man is talking to her.

21:44.000 --> 21:46.950
Sorry? He says.

21:47.000 --> 21:49.950
Are you okay?

21:50.000 --> 21:51.950
The woman stands up.

21:52.000 --> 21:54.950
No! She says.

21:55.000 --> 22:01.950
Then she looks for the mice, but she can't see them.

22:02.000 --> 22:11.950
At nine o'clock, Marcel and Henry are back at Professor Barton's flat in Old Wilton Street.

22:12.000 --> 22:14.950
They're very happy.

22:15.000 --> 22:18.950
Marcel is sitting on the table.

22:19.000 --> 22:22.950
The Shakespeare letters are in front of him.

22:23.000 --> 22:25.950
He's reading them.

22:26.000 --> 22:29.950
Henry is standing at the window.

22:30.000 --> 22:33.950
He's watching the fireworks.

22:34.000 --> 22:37.950
Suddenly, he sees a man in a brown coat.

22:38.000 --> 22:40.950
It's Professor Barton.

22:41.000 --> 22:42.950
He's coming home.

22:43.000 --> 22:45.950
The professor is smiling.

22:46.000 --> 22:51.950
Then he walks into his flat and suddenly he stops smiling.

22:52.000 --> 22:56.950
Marcel and Henry are standing behind a chair.

22:57.000 --> 22:59.950
They watch him.

23:00.000 --> 23:01.950
He goes to the safe.

23:02.000 --> 23:03.950
It's open.

23:04.000 --> 23:06.950
He looks in it and says,

23:07.000 --> 23:10.950
Oh no!

23:11.000 --> 23:15.950
Then he sees the Shakespeare letters on the table.

23:16.000 --> 23:20.950
But he puts one hand on his head.

23:21.000 --> 23:23.950
I don't understand.

23:24.000 --> 23:26.950
He looks at the safe.

23:27.000 --> 23:29.950
Then he looks at the letters.

23:30.000 --> 23:34.950
And then he looks at the safe again.

23:35.000 --> 23:37.950
Why are the letters here?

23:38.000 --> 23:40.950
He says, When?

23:41.000 --> 23:42.950
How?

23:43.000 --> 23:46.950
I don't understand.

23:47.000 --> 23:53.950
In the morning, Henry and Marcel go to the British Museum.

23:54.000 --> 23:57.950
It's a cold day and it's raining.

23:58.000 --> 24:03.950
In the museum, there are a lot of journalists and TV people.

24:04.000 --> 24:07.950
They're waiting for Professor Barton.

24:08.000 --> 24:11.950
He arrives at ten o'clock.

24:12.000 --> 24:13.950
Good morning!

24:14.000 --> 24:16.950
He says to them.

24:17.000 --> 24:20.950
He starts to talk about the Shakespeare letters.

24:21.000 --> 24:26.950
Then he gives the letters to a man from the museum.

24:27.000 --> 24:30.000
Thank you very much, Professor.

24:31.000 --> 24:35.950
Henry and Marcel are standing at the back of the room.

24:36.000 --> 24:39.950
Henry smiles at his French friend.

24:40.000 --> 24:45.000
And thank you, Marcel, he says.
